      <p>Placing a hue (H) or changing colorfulness per hue (M) moves colors away from the uniform lineup. Turning the whole lineup together keeps it uniform, though, so changes are measured against the uniform lineup <strong>turned</strong> to best match yours: what's left is the <strong>bend</strong>. How far is measured in \u0394E, how different two colors look in CAM16-UCS, and read against the palette's own scale: neighbors sit one gap apart, about 9 to 10 \u0394E. The strip at the top of Settings shows each color's bend, in gaps.</p>
